71530	{"artifactId":"PLAN-c2ba6fa62a148ed1-s5","entry":{"id":"migrated-PLAN-c2ba6fa62a148ed1-s5-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T11:07:09.420Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"plan","stage":"plan","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"p1","ref":"t1","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"src/agent/providers/ollama.ts defines wrapOllamaError, and the provider's complete/stream paths rethrow transport errors through it.","evidence":"The evidence confirms both parts of the premise. The definition is at `src/agent/providers/ollama.ts:759`: `function wrapOllamaError(err: unknown): Error {`. The grep for /wrapOllamaError/ finds four rethrow sites in the same file. Two are in the retry flow of complete: `ollama.ts:341` (`throw wrapOllamaError(err);`) and `ollama.ts:347` (`throw wrapOllamaError(lastErr);`, the throw after the last retry). The other two are in the stream paths: `ollama.ts:518` follows the `for await (const chunk of response)` loop at `ollama.ts:512`, and `ollama.ts:621` follows the loop at `ollama.ts:578`. So stream creation and stream iteration also rethrow through wrapOllamaError. One more `for await` at `ollama.ts:428` has no wrapOllamaError call close by. The premise does not claim that every stream site is wrapped, so this does not contradict it, but S005 should check that site when it routes all transport failures through ModelCallFailedError.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence confirms the premise: wrapOllamaError is defined at ollama.ts:759, and complete (341, 347) and the stream paths (518, 621) rethrow through it. No edit is needed."}},{"claimId":"p2","ref":"t1","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"A ModelCallFailedError class exists that the local provider and the retry helper in src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts 