e does not show whether its constructor accepts a cause. That is a gap in what was gathered, not a contradiction of the premise. It does not change what t1 builds, so the fix is to confirm or reword, not to redesign.","options":["Confirm the constructor at src/agent/providers/model-call-error.ts accepts a cause (e.g. `{ cause }` passed to super), and record the premise as verified, citing that line.","Extend t1: add an optional `{ cause?: unknown }` argument to ModelCallFailedError's constructor and pass it to `super(message, { cause })`, so wrapOllamaError and the retry helper can keep the original error.","Reword the premise so 'with a cause' is dropped and the defining file is named: 'A ModelCallFailedError class exported from src/agent/providers/model-call-error.ts exists, carrying a `detail`; the local provider and the retry helper in src/agent/providers/structured-output.ts can construct it.'"]}},{"claimId":"p3","ref":"t2","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"In src/analyze/context/model-failure.ts the CLI_FAILURE_TEXTS list is at :35, is matched only at message start at :75-77, and the Ollama/socket texts are matched anywhere in the message at :81-83.","evidence":"All three anchors point to the code the premise describes:\n- `src/analyze/context/model-failure.ts:35` is `const CLI_FAILURE_TEXTS: readonly string[] = [`, which is the list declaration.\n- `src/analyze/context/model-failure.ts:75` is `for (const text of CLI_FAILURE_TEXTS) {`, which is the loop that checks the CLI wordings.\n- `src/analyze/context/model-failure.ts:81` is `for (const text of OLLAMA_FAILURE_TEXTS) {`, which is the loop that checks the Ollama/socket texts.\n\nThe indexed body of isModelCallFailure in the t06.json capture supports the claim that CLI texts are matched only at the start. It computes `own = msg.replace(RETRY_PREFIX, '')` right before the loop at :75. Its comment says the provider's wording \"opens the message ... It is never matched further in.\" The S005 LLD bac