firms the premise.","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence confirms the premise: there are exactly seven source consumers, and they are the ones listed. No change is needed."}},{"claimId":"p5","ref":"t3","kind":"citation","severity":"MED","premise":"classifyOllamaError is defined at src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1019 and called from the tool loop at :793 and from runFinalStructuredEmit at :959; these are its only two callers.","evidence":"All three line anchors check out. `src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1019` reads `function classifyOllamaError(err: unknown): Error {`, which is the definition, and it does not take a `call` argument yet. `:793` reads `throw classifyOllamaError(err);`, the tool-loop call. `:959` reads `const errClass = classifyOllamaError(err);`. The evidence shows `runFinalStructuredEmit` starting at `driver.ts:868`, so line 959 plausibly sits inside it.\n\nThe claim that these are the \"only two callers\" cannot be checked from this evidence. The grep `/classifyOllamaError\\(/` hit the 50-match cap, and every match shown is under `docs/`. None of the `src/` matches were listed, so other call sites can't be ruled out. The evidence also points to a likely third reference: PLAN.md:59 names the test seam `_classifyOllamaErrorForTest` at `driver.ts:1683`, which tests call directly. A seam with that name almost certainly forwards to `classifyOllamaError`. If t3 changes the signature to `(err, call)` and updates only :793 and :959, that seam would either fail to type-check or need its own `call` value. The seam's body was not read, so this is plausible rather than confirmed.","action":"Rerun the grep limited to `src/` (for example `rg 'classifyOllamaError\\(' src/`) to list the real call sites. Read `driver.ts:1683` to see whether `_classifyOllamaErrorForTest` calls `classifyOllamaError`. If it does, change the premise to \"two production callers (:793, :959) plus the test seam at :1683\". Also make t3 explicitly update the seam's si