test.ts (asserted at :418) enumerates it.","evidence":"The evidence supports the premise. (1) It is a closed list: `src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1198` declares `export const PIPELINE_CAUSES = [`, and `driver.ts:1208` derives `export type PipelineCause = (typeof PIPELINE_CAUSES)[number];`. That gives a finite union of literals. The `as const` sits on lines 1199–1207, which the evidence does not show, but the per-literal calls in the test (`errorForPipelineCause('planner-model-failed', …)`, `'answer-prompt-missing'`, and so on at :433–:453) only type-check against a narrow literal union. (2) There is one case per member: the doc comment at `driver.ts:1195` says \"`errorForPipelineCause` has one case per member\". The function begins at `driver.ts:1264`. Its fallthrough at `driver.ts:1299` is a never-check, `throw new Error(\\`errorForPipelineCause: unhandled cause ${String(unreachable)}\\`)`, so a member with no case fails to compile. (3) The test enumerates the list: `pipeline-outcome.test.ts:418` is `assert.deepEqual([...PIPELINE_CAUSES].sort(), Object.keys(expected).sort());`, and :420 loops `for (const c of PIPELINE_CAUSES)` to call `errorForPipelineCause(c, …)` at :421. Adding 'index-state-read-failed' and 'lookup-failed' to the list therefore forces two new switch cases and two new keys in the `expected` map. That is what t4 prescribes in PLAN.md:68/:72.","action":"None needed; the evidence confirms the premise. When building t4, add both new members to the `expected` map in pipeline-outcome.test.ts, or the assertion at :418 fails.","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The premise is confirmed: a const-derived union, an exhaustive switch with a never-check at driver.ts:1299, and a test at :418 that pins the full set of members. No edit to the artifact is needed."}},{"claimId":"p9","ref":"t4","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"runShaper reads freshness directly via resolveRepoLastIndexedAt at driver.ts:357; the pipeline reads steps.lastIndexedAt at :1471 and awaits executePlan bare at :1473; REAL_PIPELINE_STEPS is at :1582 with lastIndexedAt bound to resolveRepoLastIndexedAt at :1587.","evidence":"All five anchors check out against the source. src/analyze/context/driver.ts:357 is `const currentLastIndexedAt = await resolveRepoLastIndexedAt(freshnessPathOf(scope));`, so runShaper reads freshness directly. Line 1471 is `const lastIndexedMs = await steps.lastIndexedAt(freshnessPathOf(args.scope));`, the pipeline's read. Line 1473 is `const executed = await steps.executePlan({`, a bare await, with no try wrapping shown at that line. Line 1582 is `const REAL_PIPELINE_STEPS: PipelineSteps = {`, which declares the steps object; grep confirms this is the only declaration, and the other hits at :389, :1352 and :1691 are uses. Line 1587 is `lastIndexedAt: resolveRepoLastIndexedAt,`. The premise already includes the earlier correction from PLAN.md:299-300, where the stale :1587 declaration anchor was changed to :1582.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"Every cited file:line points at the entity the premise names, so no edit is needed."}},{"claimId":"p10","ref":"t4","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"There are exactly two classifyShaperError mappings: src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts and src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts, with error-code unions AnalyzeRpcErrorCode and RunErrorCode respectively.","evidence":"grep /function classifyShaperError/ found 6 matches, and only 2 are source definitions: src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:702 (`function classifyShaperError(err: unknown): RunFailure {`) and src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:967 (`function classifyShaperError(err: unknown): AnalyzeRpcErrorPayload {`). The other 4 are in docs (PLAN.md:265, the S006 LLD.md:197-198, and a measurements t04.json snapshot). grep /classifyShaperError\\s*=/ found 0 matches, so no arrow-function or const variant exists. That confirms exactly two mappings. Both unions exist: `export type